  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Juzoor-Adopting Menstrual Hygiene</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">For localised interventions, we lean on the expertise of long-standing partners. In Gaza, our partnership with Juzoor for Health and Social Development. As a strategic Oxfam partner under our sexual and reproductive health and rights programs, Juzoor is dedicatedto improving the health and wellbeing of Palestinian families and advocating for health as a fundamental human right.
The project addresses cultural sensitivities surrounding menstruation in OPT and Gaza through culturally appropriate educationand community engagement activities. Understanding the importance of local traditions, the initiative promotes healthy and hygienic menstrual practiceswhilst respecting cultural norms. Oxfam, along with its partners, uses its extensive expertise in menstrual health to implement a behavioural change and gender transformative approach within the SL programme. A significant aspect of this strategy is the development of an extracurricular booklet that addresses gender concepts and various issues related to Menstrual Hygiene Management (MHM). Furthermore, as part of the Sexual and Reproductive Health and Rights (SRHR) projects, Oxfam, in collaboration with partners Aisha andJuzoor, has crafted several manuals targeted at providing comprehensive sexuality education. These focus particularly on menstrual health and are heavily geared towards gender considerations. Tailored for service providers, community members, and youth, these materials aim to shift negative perceptions and disseminate essential information about menstrual health in a culturally sensitive manner.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Al Juzoor Foundation for Health and</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Juzoor Foundation for Health and Social Development is a Palestinian NGO based in Jerusalem working at the national level. It is committed to improving the health and well-being of Palestinian families and to promoting health as a basic human right.
Juzoor was founded by a team of health and development professionals in 1996. The organizations was named Juzoor (roots in Arabic) to reflectthe organisations focus on the underlying socio-economic determinants of health and well-being, to reinforce thecommitment that Juzoor has made to continuing its work in Palestinian communities despite the difficult and challenging political situation.

Juzoor mission is to promote a coherent, interdisciplinary and cross-sectoral approach to improving the healthand social well-being of individuals, families and communities based on national indicators and needs. The foundation works at multiple levels with community-basedorganizations, professionals, governmental bodies, and the community at large, targeting in specific women, children, youths and service providers.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
